IMPORT prelude

-- Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) -- the dates, in one small module. It uses only the
-- built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR) and FLOOR,
-- not the daydate library.
--
-- READINGS (forks F1 and F2 in NOTES.md; the Act does not say how to count):
--   "within 3 years from the date of the relevant motor vehicle accident" (s 25(7)) and "the period of 3 years" (s 26(11))
--   end on the same day of the month three years later, or that month's last day where it is shorter (29 February
--   2016 plus three years is 28 February 2019);
--   "within 28 days of" or "after" a day (ss 35(2), 37(3), 38(3)) ends on that day plus 28;
--   "at least 28 days before leaving Australia" (s 52(1)) ends on the day of leaving less 28.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (version of 2 December 2019).
-- CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Lifetime Support Scheme Act`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the first day` `to` `the second day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the second day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`

-- The number of days from the first day to the last day, both counted (a period of participation).
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of the period from` `the first day` `to` `the last day` MEANS
    IF `the last day` `is before` `the first day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE (DATE_SERIAL `the last day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`) PLUS 1

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- Fork F1: the same day of the month n months later, or that month's last day where it is shorter.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `moved on by months` n MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the lesser of` (DATE_DAY `the day`) `and` (`the days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`)) `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the new year`    MEANS FLOOR (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month`   MEANS (`the month count` MINUS (`the new year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1
